1
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:14,540
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

2
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:31,520
Your moves!

3
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:09,420
So it's true!

4
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:11,510
Mahan!

5
00:01:11,593 --> 00:01:12,540
Please come back!

6
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:18,090
Mana!

7
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:19,440
He's gone!

8
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:24,117
Please, Pharaoh, I beg of you, use your
powers and release him from that stone!

9
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:25,080
Or can't you?

10
00:01:25,340 --> 00:01:27,177
Please tell me it's not too late!

11
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:32,420
Mana, Mahad's spirit is very much
alive, existing deep within that stone.

12
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:34,720
In fact, he's even stronger now.

13
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:38,480
My Millennium Necklace has shown me all.

14
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:42,173
He fused himself together with
his most trusted creature.

15
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:43,350
What?

16
00:01:43,433 --> 00:01:44,263
I'm confused.

17
00:01:45,180 --> 00:01:46,768
Mahad has been transformed.

18
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:49,860
He will now be known as the Dark Magician.

19
00:01:50,260 --> 00:01:51,280
Dark Magician?

20
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:55,777
My training isn't complete
and I need Master Mahad!

21
00:01:55,860 --> 00:01:58,920
I want to become an Elite Spellcaster!

22
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:00,860
I can't do it alone!

23
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:06,880
Hey, guys!

24
00:02:07,380 --> 00:02:09,040
I think we found it!

25
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:11,600
The world of the Pharaoh's memory!

26
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:14,360
Yes, you are correct.

27
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:16,640
And so, my work here is done.

28
00:02:17,060 --> 00:02:19,660
Now you must continue, on your own.

29
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:25,522
I'm sorry, but only those who were called
upon by the Pharaoh may enter this realm.

30
00:02:25,860 --> 00:02:26,690
So go.

31
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:29,337
The king of Egypt is in need of your help.

32
00:02:29,420 --> 00:02:30,250
And good luck.

33
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:32,100
You are going to need it.

34
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,680
Just one question.

35
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:36,409
How do we get out of here?

36
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:38,890
Yuki!

37
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:40,580
I was afraid of that.

38
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:52,857
Due to Mahad's carelessness, that lunatic
Bakura is more dangerous than ever.

39
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:56,880
For now, he is in control of
the Millennium Ring. Now wait.

40
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:58,837
That is yet to be confirmed.

41
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:03,817
For all we know, Bakura was buried under
rubble when the Sacred Sanctuary collapsed.

42
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:04,730
Perhaps.

43
00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:07,640
However, my ki still senses his presence.

44
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:11,480
And Isis, what does your Millennium
Item tell you about this?

45
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:13,420
Can you see Bakura's future?

46
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:15,400
Sadly, I cannot.

47
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:19,897
On behalf of the Sacred Court,
I apologize for these failures.

48
00:03:19,980 --> 00:03:21,120
Believe me,

49
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:26,440
I speak for every one of us when I say we
will not disappoint you again, Pharaoh.

50
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:28,240
I am sorry, my king.

51
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:31,480
Apologies are not necessary, Isis.

52
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:33,360
What we need are solutions.

53
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:35,291
Of course, Master Shimon.

54
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:37,957
I shall do everything in
my power to break through

55
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:40,837
the darkness that conceals
Bakura from my vision.

56
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:42,273
That is all we can ask.

57
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:46,656
Pharaoh, with all due respect,
time is of the essence.

58
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:50,020
Please allow me to lead
the hunt for Bakura.

59
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:52,084
I already have a plan in place.

60
00:03:53,020 --> 00:03:58,320
To start, all gateways to and from the
kingdom must be sealed to keep him in.

61
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:03,292
Next, every citizen must be carefully
observed since no one can be trusted.

62
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:04,290
He's right.

63
00:04:04,373 --> 00:04:07,700
Until we have more information,
everyone's a suspect.

64
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:09,780
Very well, proceed.

65
00:04:10,180 --> 00:04:12,533
So let it be written, so let it be done.

66
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:25,240
Is it me, or did we just travel
through some kind of time warp?

67
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:27,680
Just look at us.

68
00:04:27,820 --> 00:04:29,585
We stand out like sore thumbs.

69
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:30,837
Yeah, you're right.

70
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:34,260
But for some weird reason,
everyone's ignoring us.

71
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:36,080
Well, not for long.

72
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:37,677
How you doing, folks?

73
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:38,590
Jumping.

74
00:04:38,673 --> 00:04:39,503
Joey Wheeler here.

75
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:41,430
Hello.

76
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:42,610
Told you.

77
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:44,580
Hey, wait a sec.

78
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:47,680
I'm sure this nice young
girl knows who I am.

79
00:04:52,020 --> 00:04:53,180
She's a ghost!

80
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:54,420
Did you see that?

81
00:04:55,280 --> 00:04:57,120
The Millennium Puzzle is gone!

82
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:58,960
Hold on.

83
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:01,946
If we're in the world
of the Pharaoh's memory,

84
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:05,420
then it's no wonder people
can't see us, right?

85
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:10,357
We didn't exist 5,000 years ago, so
we're not really a part of this place.

86
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:11,500
Wait a sec.

87
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:15,717
Does that mean when we find the Pharaoh,
he won't be able to see us either?

88
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:16,630
Who knows?

89
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,260
But there's only one way to find out!

90
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:21,760
We have to go see him!

91
00:05:29,420 --> 00:05:34,240
Seto, do you believe that Bakura
still walks amongst us? Of course.

92
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:38,317
He controls a monster with
powers equal to an Egyptian god.

93
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:41,106
Mahad, you saw that for
yourself, did you not?

94
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:50,160
Mahad was a fool to face him, and
that is why his spirit is now sealed.

95
00:05:50,540 --> 00:05:51,893
Then what should we do?

96
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:56,720
We must strengthen our own army of
shadow creatures and take him down.

97
00:05:57,160 --> 00:06:00,257
We shall accomplish this by
extracting these beasts of

98
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:04,080
darkness from the souls of
the Egyptian people at once.

99
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:07,297
Seto, are you suggesting
we punish the innocent?

100
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:09,680
What would the pharaoh say about that?

101
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:11,190
Shadda,

102
00:06:11,273 --> 00:06:13,477
the very reason I am doing all this is to

103
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:16,266
protect the pharaoh and
the citizens of Egypt.

104
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:18,540
Guards, stop here!

105
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:25,000
And no, I am not targeting the innocent.

106
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:29,377
It is the souls of potential
criminals that I shall be seeking out.

107
00:06:29,460 --> 00:06:30,520
And punishing.

108
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:33,340
Guards, here is your mission.

109
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:35,657
You are all to scour the kingdom.

110
00:06:35,740 --> 00:06:41,500
Any villager you deem suspicious of criminal
activity is to be brought before me!

111
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:46,877
Right.

112
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:50,520
One down and five guardians to go.

113
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:54,420
And then the seven items will be mine!

114
00:07:00,300 --> 00:07:02,220
There's been a mistake!

115
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:04,670
Wake!

116
00:07:04,753 --> 00:07:05,583
Mercy!

117
00:07:05,666 --> 00:07:06,496
You must believe me!

118
00:07:06,579 --> 00:07:07,660
I'm innocent, I swear!

119
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:09,766
There is one way to find out.

120
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,680
Prepare to be judged by the
Millennium Items. Go on!

121
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:17,157
We overheard this vagrant
disrespecting the pharaoh, sir.

122
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:19,900
Well, that was certainly foolish of you.

123
00:07:20,260 --> 00:07:22,480
Shaddaa, let us see into his spirit.

124
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:28,062
Please, Millennium Key, show me
what lies within this man's heart.

125
00:07:33,340 --> 00:07:36,160
I sense an evil spark beginning to grow.

126
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,892
He appears harmless now,

127
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:43,700
but he most certainly shows potential
for greater evil, Master Seto. All right.

128
00:07:43,940 --> 00:07:45,980
This vagrant is useless to me.

129
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:47,390
Lock him up!

130
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:49,820
You're making a mistake!

131
00:07:50,180 --> 00:07:53,239
Why would you waste your
efforts on the lives of me?

132
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:56,457
There's a much more serious
threat among us, sir.

133
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:59,217
Believe me, we are all
well aware of Bakura,

134
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:02,300
and we've already taken
actions to stop him.

135
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:04,560
I'm referring to the White Dragon!

136
00:08:06,060 --> 00:08:07,180
White Dragon?

137
00:08:09,860 --> 00:08:11,340
He can't be.

138
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:13,220
It's all true!

139
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:15,640
The White Dragon stalks our town!

140
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:19,160
It emerges by night and
threatens us while we sleep!

141
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:21,556
I have heard enough.

142
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:22,677
Take him away.

143
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:24,157
Let's go! Seto?

144
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:27,500
How can you lock me up and
let the dragon roam free?

145
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:30,200
You'll be sorry for this!

146
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:42,240
The more chaos I spark, the
faster my dear bound will evolve.

147
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:46,260
Hey, can we take five?

148
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:47,760
Maybe ten?

149
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,260
Oh, come on.

150
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:51,310
You're kidding, right?

151
00:08:51,393 --> 00:08:54,360
You know I can't run on an empty stomach.

152
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:57,280
You can't do anything on an empty stomach.

153
00:08:57,720 --> 00:09:01,057
Besides, we're here to help
the Pharaoh, not to eat, Joey.

154
00:09:01,140 --> 00:09:02,620
I want a hot dog.

155
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:08,780
Did you say hot dog? Oh, great.

156
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,000
You too, Tristan?

157
00:09:10,420 --> 00:09:13,126
Remember, guys, it's
like we don't exist here.

158
00:09:13,460 --> 00:09:17,077
You two aren't even going to be able
to touch the food, let alone eat it.

159
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:19,200
Oh, no, say it ain't so.

160
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:27,320
Hey, wait, something's not right here.

161
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:28,680
What do you mean?

162
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:31,717
I mean, that guy's devouring
everything in sight.

163
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:33,337
And no one's saying a thing.

164
00:09:33,420 --> 00:09:34,538
You're right, Joey.

165
00:09:34,820 --> 00:09:37,000
Does that mean... Hey!

166
00:09:37,460 --> 00:09:39,220
You got some for us?

167
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:42,620
Help me, I'm being
attacked by a hungry ghost!

168
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:46,560
Hey, he can see us!

169
00:09:48,660 --> 00:09:49,490
No!

170
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:02,020
We got him!

171
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:07,150
Bye-bye!

172
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:10,130
Hold on.

173
00:10:10,213 --> 00:10:11,553
That girl's in trouble.

174
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:18,460
So you guys want to
pick on someone, do you?

175
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:20,057
Then pick on us!

176
00:10:20,140 --> 00:10:21,980
And then we'll pick on you!

177
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:23,100
Are you okay?

178
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:25,700
She can't hear us. That's right.

179
00:10:26,040 --> 00:10:28,569
None of these people
can hear us or see us.

180
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:31,660
No wonder these stones
don't hurt. Think, guys.

181
00:10:31,860 --> 00:10:33,272
We have to do something.

182
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:34,520
What is this about?

183
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:37,240
No way!

184
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:38,860
Double no way!

185
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:42,460
It's Kaiba!

186
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:47,820
Master Seto?

187
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:50,220
Wait, what's this?

188
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:51,880
The power within her!

189
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:53,480
It's too strong!

190
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:00,310
Shadda!

191
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:04,400
I've never felt such a
powerful spirit before. Really?

192
00:11:04,880 --> 00:11:08,360
Wait, there is something
familiar about this girl.

193
00:11:09,280 --> 00:11:11,260
Guards, she comes with us.

194
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:13,657
Give her all the food
and water she desires.

195
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:16,040
We must hurry, men! Yes, sir!

196
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:22,140
And as for all of you, leave at once, or I
shall place every one of you in shackles!

197
00:11:23,780 --> 00:11:27,700
Way to go, fake Kaiba! Look, Yugi! I know!

198
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:29,640
Kaiba has the Millennium Rod!

199
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:31,660
And that guy has the key!

200
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:33,740
It makes sense!

201
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:36,640
Kaiba was carved on that ancient tablet!

202
00:11:36,980 --> 00:11:38,686
He must work for the Pharaoh!

203
00:11:39,260 --> 00:11:41,317
Not a word about this to the Pharaoh!

204
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:46,224
We needn't concern him until we have a
full understanding of what's going on here.

205
00:11:46,500 --> 00:11:48,600
Let us return to the palace now.

206
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:52,660
Hey, did you guys hear that?

207
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:55,217
Yeah, those two guys are
on their way to the palace.

208
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:57,697
They could be our ticket
to see the pharaoh.

209
00:11:57,780 --> 00:11:58,877
What are we waiting for?

210
00:11:58,960 --> 00:11:59,790
To the palace.

211
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:01,747
I always wanted to say that.

212
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:08,220
Look at the size of this place.

213
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:10,117
It's good to be the king.

214
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:12,200
We might want to speed things up.

215
00:12:12,420 --> 00:12:13,479
Take a look, guys.

216
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:14,994
The doors are closing!

217
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:20,480
Now what are we supposed to do?

218
00:12:21,660 --> 00:12:23,400
Come on, don't sweat it.

219
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:25,377
We can walk through everything here.

220
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:28,225
And I'm sure Solid Stone
Gage are no exception.

221
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:33,840
I don't get this!

222
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:35,620
Are we invisible or not?

223
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:41,640
I hate to say it, guys, but I think
it's time for one of our famous plan Bs.

224
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:43,520
Perhaps I can help you.

225
00:12:46,020 --> 00:12:46,980
You again!

226
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,459
Hello, my friends.

227
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:52,859
You gave me quite a scare, for Buzz
is not used to people seeing him.

228
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:54,020
Let's start over.

229
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:57,442
After all, we invisible
folk must stick together.

230
00:12:57,980 --> 00:12:59,320
I'll be right down.

231
00:13:04,300 --> 00:13:05,660
Don't crush us!

232
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:07,180
How about a snack?

233
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:10,070
Finally!

234
00:13:11,020 --> 00:13:14,720
So if you're invisible like us,
then why can you touch things?

235
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:16,250
Let's see.

236
00:13:16,333 --> 00:13:17,320
It's because...

237
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:19,940
Actually, I have no idea.

238
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:23,850
Hey!

239
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:25,840
Quit eating our food!

240
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:26,997
Where are you from?

241
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:28,160
Taya, stop!

242
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:29,539
No more questions!

243
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:33,080
You see, when I get nervous, I get hungry.

244
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:34,360
You heard him!

245
00:13:34,620 --> 00:13:36,660
Stop making Bulbasa so nervous!

246
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,960
I'm trying to get us
into the palace, Nimrods.

247
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,492
What are we going to do?

248
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:44,590
No!

249
00:13:44,673 --> 00:13:45,503
Quit it, Taya!

250
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:47,700
At least I'm trying to help.

251
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:50,440
Yeah, and we're trying to eat.

252
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:54,482
I know you're in there, Pharaoh.

253
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:57,666
and I'm going to figure
out a way to help you.

254
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,220
Someone is calling out to me.

255
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:08,520
Any suspicious activity here? No, sir.

256
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:11,982
Well, I thought I heard
something, so look alive.

257
00:14:12,180 --> 00:14:14,600
The time has come on to phase two.

258
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:17,317
The shadow game has taken
an interesting twist

259
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:20,341
as the past and the future
have begun to converge.

260
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:22,437
Take the Egyptian gods.

261
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:26,755
The pharaoh can only control them
thanks to his knowledge of the future.

262
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:30,260
However, I have a power he doesn't.

263
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:38,340
Thanks to my newly
acquired Millennium Ring,

264
00:14:38,700 --> 00:14:42,320
I can enter his majesty's
palace undetected.

265
00:14:45,680 --> 00:14:48,000
Master Akhnadden, settle.

266
00:14:48,540 --> 00:14:50,500
Our mission was a success. Yes.

267
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:55,057
We searched the land for shadow creatures
dwelling within our citizens' hearts.

268
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:58,557
And our findings were greater
than I could ever have expected.

269
00:14:58,640 --> 00:14:59,816
You should be proud.

270
00:15:00,140 --> 00:15:01,180
Well, I am not.

271
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:04,077
Now release these innocent
people immediately.

272
00:15:04,160 --> 00:15:06,180
You cannot be serious. Silence.

273
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:07,820
You must do as I say.

274
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:11,260
You are starting to head
down a dangerous path, Seto.

275
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:14,460
You are a guardian, and
you must act like one.

276
00:15:14,880 --> 00:15:18,762
Free those people, for you have
disgraced the name of the Pharaoh.

277
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:19,950
Never!

278
00:15:20,300 --> 00:15:22,200
I did this to protect him.

279
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:24,753
It is the only way we can defeat Bakura.

280
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:26,820
I do not regret it at all.

281
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:31,560
But Seto, I am sorry, but there's
work to be done. Farewell.

282
00:15:34,820 --> 00:15:35,760
Seto, wait!

283
00:15:36,140 --> 00:15:37,700
You're making a mistake!

284
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:40,740
I should know.

285
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:44,160
Not long ago, I made
the same mistake myself.

286
00:15:50,300 --> 00:15:51,130
Who's there?

287
00:15:56,540 --> 00:15:57,370
Bakura!

288
00:16:01,020 --> 00:16:03,760
Is she awake? No, sir. Not yet.

289
00:16:04,280 --> 00:16:05,110
Very well.

290
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:13,220
Her face is so familiar to me.

291
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:17,020
Can this be the girl I
saw that day so long ago?

292
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:20,380
Oh, the girl with the
blue eyes and white hair.

293
00:16:30,180 --> 00:16:31,768
Well, someone's in trouble.

294
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:37,266
That prisoner's been nothing but
trouble since we captured her.

295
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:40,777
Yeah, we should have run her out
of town like the rest of them.

296
00:16:40,860 --> 00:16:42,420
Word of advice, man.

297
00:16:42,740 --> 00:16:45,220
In the next village, take no prisoners.

298
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:49,740
What are you doing? Shh.

299
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:52,220
Saving you. Let's go.

300
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:57,120
Hey, it's going somewhere.

301
00:16:58,140 --> 00:16:59,100
Come on.

302
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:01,440
After them.

303
00:17:01,780 --> 00:17:03,320
The girl is getting away.

304
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:05,960
Anyone there?

305
00:17:07,180 --> 00:17:08,010
Go.

306
00:17:08,093 --> 00:17:09,240
Then my job's done.

307
00:17:09,720 --> 00:17:12,380
Take this horse to the
next town. Trust me.

308
00:17:12,580 --> 00:17:14,697
The people there will be able to help you.

309
00:17:14,780 --> 00:17:16,839
Ride through the night if you must.

310
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:20,060
But what about you? Just go!

311
00:17:20,220 --> 00:17:22,240
Who are you? Seto!

312
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:24,900
Goodbye, Seto! Thank you!

313
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:27,500
I shall repay you someday!

314
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:33,890
No!

315
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:35,240
My village!

316
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:37,820
It must have been those scoundrels!

317
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:42,560
They'll pay for this!

318
00:17:43,940 --> 00:17:46,220
Who do you think you are?

319
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:49,940
This land is ours, and
we're taking it back!

320
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:52,677
Get out!

321
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:54,540
You don't belong here!

322
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:57,217
Look, it's that kid
who freed our prisoner!

323
00:17:57,300 --> 00:18:00,680
Tell us where she is! Leave
me alone! Get back here!

324
00:18:02,420 --> 00:18:03,250
Wait!

325
00:18:03,780 --> 00:18:07,240
Hey, get your filthy hands off! No!

326
00:18:09,300 --> 00:18:10,360
Stop this!

327
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:11,660
How could you?

328
00:18:12,140 --> 00:18:13,120
My home!

329
00:18:17,980 --> 00:18:20,480
What is that thing? A monster!

330
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:38,420
It is her.

331
00:18:38,820 --> 00:18:41,760
After all these years, she has returned.

332
00:18:43,940 --> 00:18:45,277
We meet again.

333
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:50,080
Only this time you didn't bring along any
of your friends to fight by your side.

334
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:52,040
I, on the other hand, did.

335
00:19:05,580 --> 00:19:10,286
You're not quite as impressive without
your younger counterparts to hide behind,

336
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:11,330
are you?

337
00:19:11,413 --> 00:19:13,977
I could seize your
Millennium Eye in an instant.

338
00:19:14,060 --> 00:19:19,677
but i have something more amusing
in mind after all we still

339
00:19:19,760 --> 00:19:23,477
have a score to settle perhaps
you recall a little incident

340
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:26,997
occurring in the village of
kal elna a few years ago you

341
00:19:27,080 --> 00:19:31,780
crushed my people and abandoned
your son a young boy named seto

342
00:20:14,060 --> 00:20:14,254
Thank you.
